# ── deny-by-default allowlist ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ignore everything at the root, then explicitly re-include what is genuinely
# tracked in this PUBLIC repo. This replaces the old deny-by-name scheme,
# where private skills (symlinked in from a separate private repo) were kept
# out only by listing their names in .git/info/exclude — untracked, so it
# protected nothing beyond this one clone. A forgotten name there was a
# silent leak; a forgotten name here is a directory that git still ignores,
# so a bare `git add -A` can never stage it by accident.
#
# TRAP: this must be `/*`, not `/*/`. `/*/` matches directories only, and git
# classifies a symlink-to-directory as a FILE, not a directory — so `/*/`
# would leave every private skill symlink unignored and `git add -A` would
# stage it. `/*` ignores symlinks too; the `!/<skill>/` re-includes below
# (trailing slash) only match real directories, so a symlink of the same
# name stays ignored. Verified empirically in a throwaway repo: with `/*/`
# a symlink `privskill -> target-dir` was staged by `git add -A`
# (`A  privskill`); with `/*` the same symlink was left untracked while a
# real re-included directory was staged normally.
/*

# Root files that belong to this repo.
!/.gitignore
!/.gitleaks.toml
!/README.md
!/ADAPTATION.md
!/COMPOUNDING.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/SETUP.md
!/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
!/UPDATING.md
!/LICENSE

# Root directories that belong to this repo.
!/.github/
!/bin/
!/ask-me/
!/autodev/
!/code-review/
!/contract/
!/copilot-review/
!/domain-modeling/
!/drop-review/
!/fleet-review/
!/framing-decisions/
!/grilling/
!/grill-me/
!/grill-with-docs/
!/handoff/
!/herdr/
!/implement/
!/merged/
!/meta-analysis/
!/obsidian-vault/
!/paper-outline/
!/probe/
!/resolving-merge-conflicts/
!/setup-matt-pocock-skills/
!/slack-ask/
!/slack-notify/
!/spar/
!/sync-matt-pocock-skills/
!/tdd/
!/to-spec/
!/writing-for-agents/
!/writing-git-commits/
!/writing-great-skills/

# Once re-included, the allowlist doesn't reach *inside* those directories —
# git still applies the rules below (secrets, cruft, node_modules) to their
# contents, which is what we want.

# Secrets & local config (never commit) — see SETUP.md
.slack-bot-token
*.token
settings.local.json

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local scratch — brainstorming specs, contract notes, superpowers working
# files. Never tracked in this public repo (global rule). Named explicitly
# here (not just caught by the `/*` deny-all above) so the lint check in
# bin/lint-skills.py can tell "we decided this stays ignored" from "nobody
# has decided anything about this yet" for a brand-new top-level entry.
docs/

# Externally-managed marketplace plugins installed into this skills dir
# (their own repos — install/update from their marketplaces, don't vendor here)
ui-ux-pro-max-skill/

# ── not ours ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skills that other tooling installs into this directory. They are not part of
# this repo and are not tracked. Copies of them may sit on disk; deleting them
# is a local cleanup, not a repo change.
_command/
autoplan/
benchmark/
benchmark-models/
canary/
connect-chrome/
cso/
design-consultation/
design-html/
design-review/
design-shotgun/
devex-review/
document-generate/
document-release/
health/
ios-clean/
ios-design-review/
ios-fix/
ios-qa/
ios-sync/
land-and-deploy/
landing-report/
office-hours/
pair-agent/
plan-ceo-review/
plan-design-review/
plan-devex-review/
plan-eng-review/
plan-tune/
qa/
qa-only/
retro/
setup-browser-cookies/
setup-deploy/
setup-gbrain/
skillify/
sync-gbrain/

*/node_modules/

# Skills we evaluated and chose not to own. Eight weeks of invocation logs
# recorded no use of any of them. Copies may still sit here on disk; they are
# not ours and are not tracked.
browse/
careful/
codex/
context-restore/
context-save/
diagram/
freeze/
guard/
investigate/
learn/
make-pdf/
